vms-095 (component C3 of vms-5f5): OVMX per-image module-GP prologue for the
alpha-dec-vms GCC port.

[OVMX] Teaches the TARGET_ABI_OPEN_VMS backend to establish a per-image
module-GP in the reserved register $15 at procedure entry and to address the
linkage section through it, fixing the multi-procedure GP skew that is the
crtl_rms N=7 blocker.

Root cause (docs/design-alpha-per-image-gp.md 1.1-1.3): upstream cc1 establishes
NO GP on the VMS ABI (alpha_expand_prologue's TARGET_ABI_OPEN_VMS path sets only
reg_offset; gen_prologue_ldgp is TARGET_ABI_OSF-only) and emits `.base $27', so
gas addresses every linkage/literal load relative to R27.  On entry R27 = &PDSC
(VMS Calling Standard 3.1.1/3.3); for a multi-procedure image (DECC$SHR, LIBOTS)
&PDSC of a procedure entered mid-section is skewed from the module linkage-
section base by K = that procedure's PDSC offset, so every R27-relative static
load (external addresses, large constants, linkage pairs -- and, via gas's
load_expression, even `lda reg,extern') lands K bytes off.  Single-procedure/
minimal (N<=3) images have K = 0 and are already correct.

Register choice -- $15, an OVMX divergence (Rule 8): authentic OpenVMS-Alpha uses
R29 as GP, but on this port $29 is the HARD FRAME POINTER (vms.h
HARD_FRAME_POINTER_REGNUM=29, used as the frame pointer in every stack
procedure), so $29 is NOT a free GP.  OVMX instead reserves the free call-saved
$15 (vms.h: FIXED[15] flipped 0->1; it was already CALL_USED[15]=0) and uses it
as the module-GP consistently across all OVMX-built shareables.  There is no
VSI-binary interop in play.  Because $15 is call-saved, module_GP survives every
call with NO per-call reload: an intra-module call shares the linkage section, a
cross-module/cross-image callee saves+restores the caller's $15.

Fix (docs/design-alpha-per-image-gp.md 1.4/2.1):  module_GP = &PDSC - K.
  gcc/config/alpha/vms.h
    - FIXED_REGISTERS: reserve $15 (position 15: 0->1).
  gcc/config/alpha/alpha.md
    - new UNSPECV_OVMX_GPDISP + define_insn "prologue_ovmx_gpdisp" (sets reg 15):
      emits `.ovmx_gpdisp $15,<proc>' (binutils port patch 0006-vms-4ed), which
      emits `ldah $15,0($27); lda $15,0($15)' and marks the pair
      EVAX_R_OVMX_GPDISP for the OVMX linker to patch with -K.  K = 0 => no-op.
  gcc/config/alpha/alpha.cc
    - alpha_vms_needs_module_gp(): true iff the body references any symbol or
      makes a call (== needs the linkage section).
    - alpha_compute_frame_layout: when needed, add $15 to sa_mask (so the
      caller's $15 is saved/restored by the generic loops) and force at least a
      register procedure (a frame slot for the save).
    - alpha_expand_prologue: emit gen_prologue_ovmx_gpdisp() as the LAST VMS
      prologue insn -- after the register save loop has saved the caller's $15,
      while R27 still holds &PDSC.
    - alpha_start_function: emit `.base $15' (not `.base $vms_base_regno') when a
      module-GP is established, so gas's alpha_gp_register -- the base for every
      linkage/literal load -- is the module-GP.  vms_base_regno stays the RTL
      frame/PV base (unaffected).
    - alpha_output_ovmx_gpdisp: emits the directive with the procedure's PDSC
      symbol (alpha_fnname).
  gcc/config/alpha/alpha-protos.h
    - prototype for alpha_output_ovmx_gpdisp.

The epilogue restores the caller's $15 from its frame slot (generic sa_mask
restore) before RET, so a caller resumes with its own module-GP after any call.
IMGACT's quad[1]=&PDSC cross-image linkage pair is untouched (design 3).

Clean-room (Rule 8): the module-GP model is derived only from the public VSI
OpenVMS Calling Standard (3.1.1/3.3/3.6.2) and MACRO Compiler Porting and User's
Guide (2.3.1); the `.ovmx_gpdisp' directive, EVAX_R_OVMX_GPDISP encoding, and the
$15-as-module-GP register choice are OVMX design choices, labeled [OVMX]
throughout and never presented as VMS-authentic.  No VSI/HPE source or binary was
disassembled, decompiled, or consulted.

